cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "LaserLab: Interactive Laser Physics Simulator"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-06
url: "https://bastianpd.github.io/lablaser-laser/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bastianpd/laserlab-laser/"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Educational, browser-based simulator of a four-level laser system. 
  It numerically integrates population and photon rate equations using the Runge-Kutta 
  method (RK4) to visualize energy levels, population inversion, spontaneous and stimulated 
  emission, optical gain, laser threshold dynamics, and the optical resonator cavity.
keywords:
  - laser physics
  - rate equations
  - population inversion
  - photonics
  - physics education
  - numerical simulation
  - interactive software
